{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>They shall cover with their wings over the cover.</b> This verse indicates that these cherubim were ten handbreadths tall, for from here the Sages, blessed be their memory, derived that the interior space of a sukkah must be ten handbreadths apart from the sekhakh, and the cherubim stood at a third of the mishkan — that is, at a third of the height of the mishkan, whose height was ten cubits, which is sixty handbreadths. If so, from the heads of the cherubim to the cover was ten handbreadths, which is their height. And when they said 'they stood at a third of the mishkan,' this refers to their actual bodies, but their wings extended above the third; and this is the sense of 'they shall cover with their wings over the cover' — for the space of ten handbreadths was beneath their wings down to the cover, and the sekhakh was above their heads, as mentioned at the beginning of the first chapter of Sukkah."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:16.302263990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}